# Brahmagupta's theorem — in a cyclic quadrilateral with perpendicular diagonals, the line through their intersection perpendicular to one side bisects the opposite side (source: Brahmagupta; Coxeter & Greitzer)
A B C = triangle
D = meet(perp_line(B, line(A, C)), circumcircle(A, B, C))
E = meet(line(A, C), line(B, D))
F = foot(E, line(B, C))
M = meet(line(F, E), line(A, D))
prove cong(M, A, M, D)
